{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2303660","formula":"C₇H₄Cl₃NO₃","hill":"C7H4Cl3NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":7.0,"H":4.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0,"Cl":3.0},"names":{"en":"Triclopyr","ru":"Триклопир"},"descriptions":{"en":"Triclopyr, also Trichlopyr, formally [(3,5,6-trichloropyridin-2-yl)oxy]acetic acid, is an organic compound in the pyridine family of herbicides that is used as a systemic foliar type of herbicide and, secondarily, as a fungicide. Triclopyr is an acetic acid derivative, and so a monocarboxylic acid, with a pyridyloxy substituent: specifically, a pyridin-2-yloxy group substituted by chloro groups at positions 3, 5, and 6. It functions as an herbicide by mimicking the action of the plant growth hormone auxin.","ru":"Триклопир — химическое соединение из группы пиридинкарбоновых кислот. Это пиридиновый аналог 2,4,5-трихлорфеноксиуксусной кислоты."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":41428,"mass":256.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=C(C(=NC(=C1Cl)Cl)OCC(=O)O)Cl","inchikey":"REEQLXCGVXDJSQ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-[(3,5,6-trichloro-2-pyridinyl)oxy]acetic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"41428","atoms":18,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.242,"y":-3.077,"z":0.005,"el":"Cl"},{"x":4.455,"y":0.259,"z":0.007,"el":"Cl"},{"x":2.321,"y":2.728,"z":-0.005,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-1.314,"y":-0.511,"z":-0.007,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.3,"y":1.47,"z":0.026,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.022,"y":-0.79,"z":-0.011,"el":"O"},{"x":0.501,"y":0.913,"z":-0.005,"el":"N"},{"x":0.049,"y":-0.361,"z":-0.003,"el":"C"},{"x":0.871,"y":-1.476,"z":0.002,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.089,"y":0.681,"z":-0.013,"el":"C"},{"x":2.246,"y":-1.271,"z":0.005,"el":"C"},{"x":2.75,"y":0.025,"z":0.003,"el":"C"},{"x":1.843,"y":1.073,"z":-0.002,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.553,"y":0.337,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.876,"y":1.27,"z":0.8